# The parser's reports a lost quote's line holds, held (design.md §4.17;
# defect 131's class, the recovery batches' C3, 2026-10-01; the lexer's half
# is `lost_quote.hero`).
#
# On a line that ends inside a literal that never closed, the lexer's
# `unterminated_string` or `unterminated_char` running to the line's end,
# every quote past the line's first may pair with the wrong one, and what
# the parser read there, a word after a string, a call a string took the `)`
# of, an arm's arrow, is the quote's: `g("a, "b")` cost the literal's report
# and `expected_end_of_line` at `b`. So a parser report that starts on such a
# line, at or past its first quote, is held; one before that quote stands, a
# mistake of its own, and so does every one on a line whose literal ended
# before it, the classic `'\'` at its third byte. A leaf: it reads the
# reports, and the stretches `lost_quote.lost_lines` reads from the text.
#
# | entry | called by |
# |---|---|
# | `held` | `parse.parse_source`, `parse.parse_bounded` |

use token
use diag
use lost_quote
use parse/which_arm

# `said` without the reports a lost quote's line holds past its first quote,
# the lines `lexed` names a literal never closed on.
function held(said: which_arm.Said, lexed: [diag.Diagnostic], text: str) -> which_arm.Said
    lost = lost_quote.lost_lines(lexed, text: text)

    if lost.spans.len() == 0
        return said
    return which_arm.Said(normal: kept(said.normal, lost: lost), control: kept(said.control, lost: lost))

function kept(said: [diag.Diagnostic], lost: lost_quote.Lost) -> [diag.Diagnostic]
    out: [diag.Diagnostic] @= []

    for d in said
        if !lost_quote.holds(lost, at: d.span.start)
            out @ out.push(d)

    return out

## Tests

test "a report past a lost quote's first quote on its line is held, and one before it stands"
    text = "    print(g(\"a, \"b\"))\n    x = 1 2\n"
    lexed = [diag.new_diagnostic(code: "unterminated_string", message: "m", span: token.Span(start: 18, end: 21))]
    past = diag.new_diagnostic(code: "expected_end_of_line", message: "m", span: token.Span(start: 17, end: 18))
    before = diag.new_diagnostic(code: "expected_args_close", message: "m", span: token.Span(start: 4, end: 9))
    below = diag.new_diagnostic(code: "expected_end_of_line", message: "m", span: token.Span(start: 32, end: 33))
    said = held(which_arm.Said(normal: [past, before, below], control: [past]), lexed: lexed, text: text)
    assert said.normal.len() == 2
    assert said.normal[0].span.start == 4
    assert said.normal[1].span.start == 32
    assert said.control.len() == 0
